# Folder-per-Component

Every component lives in its own directory. Never leave flat `.tsx` files in a parent folder.

## Folder layout

```
ComponentName/
├── ComponentName.tsx      # UI logic, named export only
├── index.ts               # export { ComponentName } from './ComponentName';
├── ComponentName.module.css   # optional
└── ComponentName.test.tsx   # optional
```

## Rules

- **Never** use `index.tsx` for component logic — keeps Ctrl+P search precise.
- **Always** add `index.ts` as the only public gateway; imports use the folder path:
  `import { ProductCard } from '@/features/products/components/ProductCard'`
- Use **named exports** in the `.tsx` file.
- Co-locate `.module.css` and `.test.tsx` in the same folder.

## Example

```tsx
// ProductCard/ProductCard.tsx
export function ProductCard() { ... }

// ProductCard/index.ts
export { ProductCard } from './ProductCard';
```
